## STAGE 3: NGROK (PUBLIC INTERNET)

### What happened:
- Exposed your Docker container to the entire internet
- Used ngrok tunnel to create public URL
- Teacher can access from anywhere

### Commands:
```powershell
# 1. Download ngrok from ngrok.com
# 2. Authenticate (sign up free)
ngrok config add-authtoken YOUR_TOKEN

# 3. Create tunnel to your Docker container
ngrok http 8080
# Now you get a public URL: https://abc123.ngrok.io

# Teacher accesses:
# https://abc123.ngrok.io/Employee
```

